<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $20.5 mln Jan 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $20.5 mln Jan 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $20.5 million surplus on Jan 13 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 13</p>
<p>Exports: $173.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $199.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $285.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $239.6 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $20.5 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.593 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.727 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.052 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.646 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $272 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
